## Plan

## Approach

- Mirror `review.voters` for `design.plan_voters`: three Codex-primary voters with labels `codex-validity`, `codex-plan-fidelity`, and `codex-pragmatism`.
- Refactor `plan_review_panel.dispatch_voters` to mirror `agent_voters.dispatch_voters` (#5837): all launched slots in one waterfall manifest, semantic `VOTER_N_TOOL` labels from policy bindings, and a dedicated Claude launch only on the both-externals-down floor.
- Resolve all three voter slots through the same `_semantic_label` + `_state_from_bindings` pattern as `agent_voters`: derive `voter_N_tool`, output paths, and per-slot prompt files from `bind_manifest_slot_outputs`, then thread those semantic tools through `_parse_rate_retry`, voter-status-block emission, and final `VOTER_N_TOOL` KVs (reuse `_emit_final_kvs` or an equivalent helper). Use raw `claude` only on the both-externals-down floor branch.
- Keep the both-externals-down floor as one Claude voter.
- Add a small HARD-only per-panel, per-archetype Codex role override.
- Use row-level `model_role` in panel manifests so a HARD panel can mix `default` and `review` Codex roles without duplicating archetypes; assert `resolved_model` on manifest rows matches role (`CODEX_DEFAULT_MODEL` vs `CODEX_REVIEW_MODEL_DEFAULT`).
- Pin all dynamic Codex reviewer rows to the `review` role.
- On TRIVIAL code review, always emit `dyn-cursor` when Cursor is available; drop only `dyn-codex`.
- Update voter calibration fallback labels for new design voter slots.
- Update docs, topology rows, prompt-invariant harness, and round-loop integration mocks in lockstep.

